    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.57). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive confluence of positive factors against Sugano, including an elite 19% SP skill boost and a 14% park factor, cementing his status as our premier start. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** enjoys a prime #3 order slot and a favorable matchup against Cantillo, making him a cornerstone of today\u2019s offensive strategy. We are also monitoring the speed element closely; **Henry Bolte** (65.39) and **Nasim Nunez** (61.05) remain critical for our stolen base targets. **Henry Bolte** specifically gains significant leverage from an aggressive leadoff role and a 19% boost from the matchup against Bradford, while **Nasim Nunez** provides unexpected value as a bottom-of-the-order spark plug, maintaining a strong efficiency score despite his #9 placement.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench involved **Luis Lara**, who just missed the cut with a 51.07 score. While **Luis Lara** possesses the switch-hitting versatility and positive wind conditions that could have warranted a start, he ultimately lost out to the higher floor provided by **Heliot Ramos** (51.19), whose status as an elite base-stealer against a slower pitcher delivery gives him the edge in our scarcity-focused build. We must remain cautious with **Heliot Ramos**, as the matchup against Detmers remains risky due to the pitcher\u2019s 3.40 xERA; he is the most volatile asset in our current configuration. We are also tracking official lineups for **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**; should any of these stars be scratched, we are prepared to pivot to the depth provided by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** or **Wade Meckler** to ensure our daily game caps are utilized effectively.",
